Meddyan wrote:
> Yesterday I was playing a few wizards, and was thinking about what the
> best possible start-up inventory could be. Heres what I would go for
> if I could control the RNG (assuming a magic marker and blind fold as
> well):
>
> Blessed scrolls of charging, enchant armour, and genocide.

I'd rather have blessed enchant weapon, blessed charging, and blessed
enchant armor, but your choices are pretty darn good as well.


> For potions, I'd take 2 blessed gain abilities and 1 holy water.

If the marker's already blessed, 1 blessed full healing, 1 cursed gain
level, and 1 blessed gain level.  The carrying capacity is easy to
deal with by good inventory management, and hungerless casting just
isn't a big deal--I'm almost always more concerned with how to lose my
satiated status than how to avoid hungry.

> I'd take a spellbook of Identify

It's convenient. Among others, charm monster and create monster are
both _far_ nicer.  Magic missile is clearly better than identify as
well, but not up with those first 2.  Charm monster may be the closest
thing to a "Welcome to nethack, you ascend now!" object outside of a /
wishing.

> For rings, there are quite a lot of goods ones to choose from. I'd
> probably settle for Teleport Control (convience + emergency, once you
> find a nymph or too) and Free Action.

Free action is almost completely worthless, and conflict is the best
ring in the game.  Telecontrol is nice.  Conflict and regeneration
would be my picks, but conflict and telecontrol would be pretty close.

The only rings worse than free action early on are aggravate monster,
slow digestion, and maybe polymorph--I'd definitely rather have even
an uncursed ring of hunger than free action, and things like
regeneration, invisibility, poison resistance, levitation, searching,
stealth, sustain ability, any other resistance, gain str/con,
polycontrol, etc are all _much_ better.  Free action is good in the
endgame for avoiding a specific situation, but it's a very long time
before it's even moderately useful.  And it's mostly useful then
because you've got good alternatives for all the other rings, not
because it's really that useful itself.

> Finally, a wand of death, for getting you out of almost any fight that
> has turned bad. A wand of cancellation might be handy too, mainly so
> you have knowledge of it (help prevent accidents), and lets you create
> holy water/blank scrolls as soon as you find the junk to blank.

I'll take fire, digging, lightning, speed, cold, sleep, or
teleportation over cancellation/polymorph, but those 2 are both pretty
good too.



